  "notes": "{帰|かえ}す means to send someone back or let them go home. The subject causes or allows someone to return to their original location.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {帰|かえ}る (intransitive, to return/go home)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{帰|かえ}している means 'is in the process of sending back' (ongoing action), not a resultant state.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～を{家|いえ}に{帰|かえ}す: to send ~ home\n- ～を{帰|かえ}してあげる: to let ~ go home\n- {早|はや}く{帰|かえ}す: to send home early\n\nDON'T CONFUSE:\n- {帰|かえ}す: to send back (people)\n- {返|かえ}す: to return, give back (objects, money)\n- {戻|もど}す: to return, put back (objects to original position)",
